<title>FRANCE: HORSE RACING-RESULTS OF FEATURE RACES AT MAISONS-LAFFITTE.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-RESULTS OF FEATURE RACES AT MAISONS-LAFFITTE.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of feature races at</p>
<p>Maisons-Laffitte on Friday:</p>
<p>Prix Djebel for three-year-old colts and geldings run over</p>
<p>seven furlongs (1.4 kms):</p>
<p>1. Fantastic Fellow (ridden by Olivier Peslier)</p>
<p>2. Nombre Premier (Gerald Mosse)</p>
<p>3. Inkatha (Dominique Boeuf)</p>
<p>Six ran.</p>
<p>Distances: Three quarters of a length, two lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by The Thoroughbred Corporation and trained in</p>
<p>England by Clive Brittain.</p>
<p>Value to winner: $26,397.</p>
<p>Pari-Mutuel (to a one-franc stake): Win 3.20; Places 1.90</p>
<p>1.80; Straight forecast 9.00</p>
<p>Prix Imprudence for three-year-old fillies run over seven</p>
<p>furlongs (1.4 kms):</p>
<p>1. Pas De Response (Freddie Head)</p>
<p>2. Barnata (Sylvain Guillot)</p>
<p>3. Psylla (Olivier Peslier).</p>
<p>Three ran.</p>
<p>Distances: Two and a half lengths, three lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by the Wertheimer Brothers and trained in</p>
<p>France by Criquette Head (Fr).</p>
<p>Value to winner: $26,397.</p>
<p>Pari-Mutuel: Win; 1.30; Straight forecast 1.40.</p>
</text>
